 is still a  completely open problem in reinforcement  learning maybe not completely open it is  a pressing and central challenge in  modern reinforcement learning is how to  take what you learn and generalize how  to take a step back and use your  expertise in one problem in one  environment to solve another problem in  another environment that would be real  general artificial intelligence we're a  long way away from that so the good news  is that that's not going to be solved in  five years or ten years that's a  hundreds of year problem but it's really  exciting because that means you know  there's work to be done important  interesting work in the field of  reinforcement learning for you know  lifetimes of research to be done in  figuring out how to improve these  systems figuring out how to learn faster  and better both from from what you're  you're learning and the reward structure  of this problem but also from what  you've learned in other problems okay  thank you so much for watching
 

